The bridge-free typed connection claims both close, but my stronger reviewer-authored claims over the exact `Val`-typed `isInt`-guarded domain do not: the backend cannot turn `isInt(A) == true` into an `Int` sort cast. This is not a false-rule witness—every ground `Val` satisfying `isInt` is an injected integer, and the bridge agrees with fixed `MPY-INT` there—but it is a real machine-checked connection limitation that I will carry into the verdict. I’m now producing the exhaustive declaration/rule inventory and the construct-to-semantics map.
